<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Losslessness</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let the current state of the sequence be <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(t_{0})=X^{\prime};X_{k}(t_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(t_{0})=X^{\prime};X_{k}(t_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. We wish to show that when the denoising progresses from <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}\rightarrow t_{0}-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}\rightarrow t_{0}-2</annotation></semantics></math>, we achieve the same result whether we had used only the true (target) probabilities or accepted a draft block using Spiffy and skipped to timestep <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}-2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, define the process of sampling the next state of a block <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> from some probability distribution <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> as a function <span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Next(<math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>. This is simply the process of using <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> to performing ranking and picking of token positions to be unmasked in <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> described in <span id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Steps 1-4</span> of Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4.2 Verification ‣ 4 Method ‣ Spiffy: Multiplying Diffusion LLM Acceleration via Lossless Speculative Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and is common to both speculative and non-speculative implementations.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Vanilla decoding output: </span> Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{*}_{k}(t_{0}-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{*}_{k}(t_{0}-2)</annotation></semantics></math> be the final state of the sequence with no speculation. From <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}\rightarrow t_{0}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}\rightarrow t_{0}-1</annotation></semantics></math>, we may obtain the next state as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\text{TD}}(t_{0}-1)\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>TD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\text{TD}}(t_{0}-1)\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad p_{\theta}\left(X_{k}(t_{0}-1)\mid X^{\prime};X_{k}(t_{0})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad p_{\theta}\left(X_{k}(t_{0}-1)\mid X^{\prime};X_{k}(t_{0})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{k}(t_{0}-1)\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{k}(t_{0}-1)\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\texttt{Next}\left(X_{k}(t_{0}),p_{\text{TD}}(t_{0}-1)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Next</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>TD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\texttt{Next}\left(X_{k}(t_{0}),p_{\text{TD}}(t_{0}-1)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This state becomes the true state of the block and inference is performed on it once more by the dLLM to advance to <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}-2</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\text{TD}}(t_{0}-2)\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>TD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\text{TD}}(t_{0}-2)\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad p_{\theta}\left(X_{k}(t_{0}-2)\mid X^{\prime};X_{k}(t_{0}-1)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad p_{\theta}\left(X_{k}(t_{0}-2)\mid X^{\prime};X_{k}(t_{0}-1)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{k}^{*}(t_{0}-2)\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{k}^{*}(t_{0}-2)\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\texttt{Next}\left(X_{k}(t_{0}-1),p_{\text{TD}}(t_{0}-2)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Next</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>TD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\texttt{Next}\left(X_{k}(t_{0}-1),p_{\text{TD}}(t_{0}-2)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Spiffy output: </span> Let <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{k}^{+}(t_{0}-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k}^{+}(t_{0}-2)</annotation></semantics></math> be the state of the sequence if we first accept a draft block <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}^{m}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}^{m}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> at timestep <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> using Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4.2 Verification ‣ 4 Method ‣ Spiffy: Multiplying Diffusion LLM Acceleration via Lossless Speculative Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, then treat it as the true block, and then continue to the next iteration of the algorithm where we perform unmasking once more.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">First, in the case of speculation, we also sample <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{k}(t_{0}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k}(t_{0}-1)</annotation></semantics></math> as usual in <span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Steps 1-4</span> as is done in (<a href="#A1.E16" title="In A.1 Proof ‣ Appendix A Proof of Losslessness ‣ Spiffy: Multiplying Diffusion LLM Acceleration via Lossless Speculative Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>). The next step of the algorithm is to check for acceptance or rejection.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 1 (rejection)</span>: For any of the drafts <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\{1,\cdots,D\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\{1,\cdots,D\}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}_{k}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}_{k}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is rejected, the algorithm continues to the next available draft and checks again for acceptance or rejection. If all drafts are rejected, we simply break and output <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{k}(t_{0}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k}(t_{0}-1)</annotation></semantics></math> as the true block state. At this point, in the next iteration, we will call the dLLM once more and this state <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{k}(t_{0}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k}(t_{0}-1)</annotation></semantics></math> will be used to compute <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{TD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>TD</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{TD}}</annotation></semantics></math> as is done in (<a href="#A1.E17" title="In A.1 Proof ‣ Appendix A Proof of Losslessness ‣ Spiffy: Multiplying Diffusion LLM Acceleration via Lossless Speculative Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>). Thus, we obtain <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{k}^{+}(t_{0}-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k}^{+}(t_{0}-2)</annotation></semantics></math> in the same way and from the same distribution as <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{k}^{*}(t_{0}-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k}^{*}(t_{0}-2)</annotation></semantics></math> and thus they are equal.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 2 (acceptance)</span>: If <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}_{k}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}_{k}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is accepted. We now set <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{TD}}\leftarrow p^{m}_{\text{DD}}(t_{m}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>TD</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>DD</mtext><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{TD}}\leftarrow p^{m}_{\text{DD}}(t_{m}-1)</annotation></semantics></math> and restart the algorithm. In this next step, we sample from this distribution to obtain</p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{k}^{+}(t_{0}-2)\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{k}^{+}(t_{0}-2)\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\quad\texttt{Next}\left(\hat{X}_{k}^{m}(t_{m}-1),p_{\text{DD}}^{m}(t_{m})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Next</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>DD</mtext><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\quad\texttt{Next}\left(\hat{X}_{k}^{m}(t_{m}-1),p_{\text{DD}}^{m}(t_{m})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Since we previously had acceptance, we first have that <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{m}==t_{0}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{m}==t_{0}-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, we have that <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}_{k}^{m}==X_{k}(t_{0}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}_{k}^{m}==X_{k}(t_{0}-1)</annotation></semantics></math> from the acceptance condition. So we see that:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{DD}}^{m}(t_{m}-1)=p_{\text{DD}}^{m}(t_{0}-2)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>DD</mtext><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>DD</mtext><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{DD}}^{m}(t_{m}-1)=p_{\text{DD}}^{m}(t_{0}-2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">and, since by definition</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{DD}}^{m}(t_{m}-1)=p_{\theta}\left(X_{k}(t_{m}-1)\mid X^{\prime};\hat{X}_{k}^{m}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>DD</mtext><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{DD}}^{m}(t_{m}-1)=p_{\theta}\left(X_{k}(t_{m}-1)\mid X^{\prime};\hat{X}_{k}^{m}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p">we have that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\text{DD}}^{m}(t_{0}-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>DD</mtext><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\text{DD}}^{m}(t_{0}-2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{\theta}\left(X_{k}(t_{0}-2)\mid X^{\prime};X_{k}(t_{0}-1)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{\theta}\left(X_{k}(t_{0}-2)\mid X^{\prime};X_{k}(t_{0}-1)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{\text{TD}}(t_{0}-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>TD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{\text{TD}}(t_{0}-2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.4" class="ltx_p">So, in reality, we sample</p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\text{DD}}^{m}(t_{0}-2)\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>DD</mtext><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\text{DD}}^{m}(t_{0}-2)\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad p_{\theta}\left(X_{k}(t_{0}-2)\mid X^{\prime};X_{k}(t_{0}-1)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad p_{\theta}\left(X_{k}(t_{0}-2)\mid X^{\prime};X_{k}(t_{0}-1)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad=p_{\text{TD}}(t_{0}-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>TD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad=p_{\text{TD}}(t_{0}-2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
